# handback.sh on the kind lab, recorded on 2026-09-30, straight after the run
# in run-2026-09-30.log on the same clusters (KIND=klab, PREFIX=klab-0930-m2),
# with cub kubara built from the handback branch (0.3.0-dev).
#
# Before it, Kubara's hub read every release from ConfigHub, argobot ran on the
# hub, and ConfigHub had released three metrics-server replicas to both
# clusters. The platform's Git repository still held the chart's default, one.
# The whole script took about a minute.
#
# What to look for:
# - handback.sh checks each of the 8 Applications against Kubara's Git render
#   first: each prunes nothing (step 0/4).
# - Every Application reads Git and syncs a Git commit (steps 1/4 and 4/4). A
#   sync the hub's argocd Application started from ConfigHub is stopped.
# - Git delivers what it holds: metrics-server goes back to one replica.
# - Secrets: a hash of each Secret's data on both clusters, before and after.
#   handback removes two of its own, argobot's credential and the gateway's.
#   The other 16 are unchanged. The two removed are shown by name only here;
#   the run printed their hashes too, which are cut from this log.
# - Pruning: of the 284 objects the Applications managed before, none was
#   pruned. Nine are new: Helm hooks (Jobs and their RBAC) that Argo CD runs on
#   a sync from Git and keeps as hooks.
# - A new commit, two replicas on the hub, reaches it from Git (section 4).
#   The Deployment was still rolling out its second pod when the log was taken.
#
# Handing the hub over again was run on an earlier lab the same day
# (PREFIX=klab-0930), after the same handback. The re-run of handover.sh
# released nothing new, found that each Application prunes nothing, and every
# Application read ConfigHub again:
#   == 4/6 Release each variant, stage by stage: promote, approve, publish
#   cert-manager: every variant has a release; later changes go through your own change orders
#   ...
#   argo-cd: every variant is released
#   == 5/6 Hand the hub to ConfigHub (your hub cluster)
#   hub-cert-manager: prunes nothing
#   ... (all eight)
#   hub-argocd reads oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-argo-cd-hub
#   exit 0

######## KIND=klab PREFIX=klab-0930-m2 bash examples/kind-lab/handback.sh


