hub-cert-manager       Synced   Degraded      <none>   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-m2-cert-manager-hub
hub-homer-dashboard    Synced   Healthy       <none>   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-m2-homer-dashboard-hub
hub-metrics-server     Synced   Healthy       <none>   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-m2-metrics-server-hub
hub-traefik            Synced   Progressing   <none>   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-m2-traefik-hub
spoke-cert-manager     Synced   Degraded      <none>   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-m2-cert-manager-spoke
spoke-metrics-server   Synced   Healthy       <none>   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-m2-metrics-server-spoke
spoke-traefik          Synced   Progressing   <none>   oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/klab-0930-m2-traefik-spoke

metrics-server runs 3 replicas on hub and 3 on spoke, as ConfigHub released; Git holds the chart's default, 1.
18 Secrets on the two clusters; 284 objects the Applications manage.

== 2. Hand the hub back to Git

$ cub kubara handback platform --prefix klab-0930-m2 --out confighub --capabilities hub=kind-klab-hub --capabilities spoke=kind-klab-spoke
Wrote confighub/handback.sh. These ApplicationSets will read Kubara's Git again:
  argocd
  cert-manager
  homer-dashboard
  metrics-server
  traefik
The AppProject hub-dev will permit Kubara's sources only.
It first checks that none of these would prune anything: hub-argocd, hub-cert-manager, spoke-cert-manager, hub-homer-dashboard, hub-metrics-server, spoke-metrics-server, hub-traefik, spoke-traefik

Next
  less confighub/handback.sh
  HUB_CONTEXT=<kubectl context of Kubara's hub> bash confighub/handback.sh

$ bash confighub/handback.sh

