$ kubectl --context kind-klab-hub get namespace argobot --ignore-not-found

== 4. A new commit in Git reaches the hub

$ git -C platform add -A

$ git -C platform -c user.name=kubara-lab -c user.email=lab@example.com commit -q -m 'Two metrics-server replicas on hub'

$ kubectl --context kind-klab-hub -n argocd get application hub-metrics-server -o custom-columns=APPLICATION:.metadata.name,SYNC:.status.sync.status,HEALTH:.status.health.status,REVISION:.status.sync.revisions[1]
APPLICATION          SYNC     HEALTH        REVISION
hub-metrics-server   Synced   Progressing   8922f65f9cff48e66ce1a0632ffa78e44bd0a219

$ git -C platform rev-parse HEAD
8922f65f9cff48e66ce1a0632ffa78e44bd0a219

$ kubectl --context kind-klab-hub -n metrics-server get deploy metrics-server
NAME             READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE
metrics-server   1/2     2            1           32m

Done. Kubara's hub delivers from Git again. ConfigHub keeps every Space and
release; bash confighub/handover.sh hands the hub over again.
